    "sourcePrompt": "Three-column time-echo split effect over backgroundVideo. Canvas-based rendering (no multiple video playback) to prevent black frames. THREE split events in this 30s clip at fixed times\n═══ HTML STRUCTURE ═══\n#mainVideo: backgroundVideo element, plays normally, position:absolute, width:100%, height:100%, object-fit:cover, z-index:1\n#auxVideo1: same src as backgroundVideo, muted, preload:auto, DO NOT call .play(), position:fixed, left:-9999px, width:1px, height:1px. Used only for currentTime seek\n#auxVideo2: identical to #auxVideo1\n#splitCanvas: position:absolute, top:0, left:0, width:100%, height:100%, z-index:2, display:none initially\n#detectCanvas: position:fixed, left:-9999px, width:64px, height:36px. Hidden. Used for scene-cut luminance detection\n#barLeft: position:absolute, z-index:3, left:calc(33.33% - 5px), top:0, width:10px, height:100%, background:#000, box-shadow:0 0 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.45)\n#barRight: position:absolute, z-index:3, left:calc(66.67% - 5px), top:0, width:10px, height:100%, background:#000, box-shadow:0 0 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.45)\n#splitWrapper: wraps #splitCanvas + #barLeft + #barRight. position:absolute, top:0, left:0, width:100%, height:100%, opacity:0, visibility:hidden, z-index:2\n═══ SPLIT ENTER — trigger at t=3.0s, t=12.0s, t=22.0s ═══\n1. Set #splitWrapper visibility:visible, then animate opacity 0→1 over 0.15s easeOut (CSS transition)\n2. Animate #barLeft: transform translateX(-100%)→translateX(0), 0.15s easeOut\n3. Animate #barRight: transform translateX(+100%)→translateX(0), 0.15s easeOut\n4. Set #splitCanvas display:block\n5. Fade #mainVideo opacity 1→0 over 0.15s\n6. Start canvas rAF loop (see below)\n7. Record holdStartTime = performance.now()\n═══ CANVAS rAF LOOP (while split active) ═══\nconst ctx = splitCanvas.getContext('2d')\nResize splitCanvas.width/height to match container pixel dimensions each frame if needed\nconst W = splitCanvas.width, H = splitCanvas.height\n// Seek aux videos (no play call)\nauxVideo1.currentTime = Math.min(mainVideo.currentTime + 0.3, mainVideo.duration - 0.01)\nauxVideo2.currentTime = Math.min(mainVideo.currentTime + 0.6, mainVideo.duration - 0.01)\n// Draw three columns — each column shows full-width video cropped to its third\nctx.drawImage(mainVideo,  0,       0, W, H,   0,       0, W/3, H);  // left col: crop left third of frame\nctx.drawImage(auxVideo1,  W/3,     0, W/3, H, W/3,     0, W/3, H);  // center col: crop center third\nctx.drawImage(auxVideo2,  W*2/3,   0, W/3, H, W*2/3,   0, W/3, H);  // right col: crop right third\n// Scene-cut detection on #detectCanvas\nconst dCtx = detectCanvas.getContext('2d')\ndCtx.drawImage(mainVideo, 0, 0, 64, 36)\nconst pixels = dCtx.getImageData(0, 0, 64, 36).data\nlet lum = 0\nfor (let i = 0; i < pixels.length; i += 4) lum += (pixels[i] + pixels[i+1] + pixels[i+2]) / 3\nlum /= (pixels.length / 4)\nif (typeof prevLum !== 'undefined' && Math.abs(lum - prevLum) > 18) { triggerExit(); return; }\nprevLum = lum\n// Fallback exit after 4s\nif (performance.now() - holdStartTime > 4000) { triggerExit(); return; }\nrafId = requestAnimationFrame(loop)\n═══ SPLIT EXIT (triggerExit function) ═══\ncancelAnimationFrame(rafId)\n// Animate #splitWrapper as single unit: opacity 1→0, 0.15s easeIn. ONE transition on parent only\nsplitWrapper.style.transition = 'opacity 0.15s ease-in'\nsplitWrapper.style.opacity = '0'\n// Simultaneously slide bars out\nbarLeft.style.transition = 'transform 0.15s ease-in'\nbarLeft.style.transform = 'translateX(-100%)'\nbarRight.style.transition = 'transform 0.15s ease-in'\nbarRight.style.transform = 'translateX(100%)'\n// Fade main video back in\nmainVideo.style.transition = 'opacity 0.15s ease-in'\nmainVideo.style.opacity = '1'\nsetTimeout(() => {\nsplitWrapper.style.visibility = 'hidden'\nsplitCanvas.style.display = 'none'\nprevLum = undefined\n}, 150)\n═══ BETWEEN EVENTS ═══\n#splitWrapper: visibility:hidden, opacity:0. #mainVideo: opacity:1, playing. No artifacts\nNO text, NO